		(render_cache "A LiPo/Li-Ion 3.7V battery can go here and connect to the J5 connector\nbelow in the bottom left. A battery protection circuit is included, so you\nmay use unprotected batteries if you really wanted to.\n\nThe circuit is designed to use battery power when independent and\nUSB-C power when plugged in. Any USB-C cable capable of supplying\n5V will charge this device, it should be safe with USBC-PD but it will only\nask for 5V.\n\nThe screen will connect via J2, and its LED panel to J3. The LED driver\ncircuit is optional, but useful even with a non-frontlit display in case you\nwant to take advantage of the accessory port in the top right. The driver\nwill supply 15mA and up to 29V to the LED+ pins, completing the circuit\nthrough C-/W- depending on software toggle. The 15mA limit can be\ntuned via R37 (value is 82ohm).\n\nThe ESP32-S3 connects via native USB 2.0, and can enter programming\nmode by holding BOOT, pressing RST, and letting go of both."
